#!/bin/sh
# wifi: the phone's Wi-Fi, with wpa_supplicant and udhcpc running as Flare
# programs over the driver host's Linux (its wcn36xx driver has the radio;
# kernel/src/linux/remote.rs carries their sockets there).
#
#   wifi scan                   networks in range
#   wifi connect SSID [PASS]    join (WPA-PSK with PASS, open without), then DHCP
#   wifi status                 state and address
#   wifi off
IF=${WIFI_IF:-wlan0}
CONF=/etc/wpa_supplicant.conf
RUN=/var/run/wpa_supplicant
cli() { wpa_cli -p $RUN -i $IF "$@"; }
start() {
    if ! [ -e /sys/class/net/$IF ]; then
        echo "wifi: no $IF (is Wi-Fi up? the driver host's log says: linuxdrv: network ...)" >&2
        exit 1
    fi
    if ! cli ping > /dev/null 2>&1; then
        mkdir -p $RUN
        [ -e $CONF ] || printf 'ctrl_interface=%s\nupdate_config=1\n' $RUN > $CONF
        wpa_supplicant -B -D nl80211 -i $IF -c $CONF > /tmp/wpa_supplicant.log 2>&1
        i=0
        while ! cli ping > /dev/null 2>&1 && [ $i -lt 50 ]; do usleep 100000; i=$((i + 1)); done
    fi
}
case "$1" in
    scan)
        start
        cli scan > /dev/null
        sleep 4
        cli scan_results | tail -n +2 | awk -F'\t' '{ printf "%-32s %s dBm  %s\n", $5, $3, $4 }'
        ;;
    connect)
        [ -n "$2" ] || { echo "usage: wifi connect SSID [PASSWORD]" >&2; exit 2; }
        start
        cli remove_network all > /dev/null
        id=$(cli add_network)
        cli set_network $id ssid "\"$2\"" > /dev/null
        if [ -n "$3" ]; then
            cli set_network $id psk "\"$3\"" > /dev/null
        else
            cli set_network $id key_mgmt NONE > /dev/null
        fi
        cli enable_network $id > /dev/null
        cli select_network $id > /dev/null
        cli save_config > /dev/null
        i=0
        while ! cli status | grep -q "wpa_state=COMPLETED" && [ $i -lt 30 ]; do sleep 1; i=$((i + 1)); done
        if ! cli status | grep -q "wpa_state=COMPLETED"; then
            echo "wifi: could not join '$2' ($(cli status | grep wpa_state))" >&2
            exit 1
        fi
        echo "wifi: joined '$2'"
        udhcpc -i $IF -n -q -t 8 -s /usr/share/udhcpc/default.script
        ;;
    status)
        start
        cli status | grep -E "^(ssid|wpa_state|ip_address|freq)="
        ;;
    off)
        cli terminate > /dev/null 2>&1
        ifconfig $IF down 2>/dev/null
        echo "wifi: off"
        ;;
    *)
        sed -n '6,10p' "$0" | sed 's/^# *//'
        ;;
esac
